How can I create a MATLAB function that takes a matrix of numbers and gradually decreases each number by 2, then exponentially increases them by 3? The function should return the final matrix.
Here is an example:
Input: [1 2 3; 4 5 6; 7 8 9]
Output: [0.1111 0.2963 0.5926; 2.7037 9.2593 27; 84.1111 229.3704 656.1]
To solve this problem, you can use nested for loops to iterate through the matrix and apply the necessary calculations to each number. Here is the MATLAB code to implement the function:
function result = gradually_exponentially(matrix)
    [m, n] = size(matrix);
    result = zeros(m, n);
    for i = 1:m
        for j = 1:n
            num = matrix(i, j);
            num -= 2;
            num = exp(num);
            num *= 3;
            result(i, j) = num;
        end
    end
end
