What is the formula for calculating the correlation coefficient between two variables in a data set? Use the following code snippet to help illustrate your answer:
```
const xValues = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
const yValues = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10];
function correlationCoefficient(x, y) {
  const n = x.length;
  const meanX = x.reduce((a, b) => a + b) / n;
  const meanY = y.reduce((a, b) => a + b) / n;
  const xDeviation = x.map(value => value - meanX);
  const yDeviation = y.map(value => value - meanY);
  const numerator = xDeviation.reduce((a, b, index) => a + b * yDeviation[index], 0);
  const xSquareSum = xDeviation.reduce((a, b) => a + b ** 2, 0);
  const ySquareSum = yDeviation.reduce((a, b) => a + b ** 2, 0);
  const denominator = Math.sqrt(xSquareSum * ySquareSum);
  const correlation = numerator / denominator;
  return correlation;
}
console.log(`Correlation coefficient between xValues and yValues: ${correlationCoefficient(xValues, yValues)}`);
```
Remember to explain the meaning and significance of the correlation coefficient in relation to the variables in the data set.

