You have been hired to manage a new social media platform that only allows 9-letter usernames. The platform is designed for people who have an insatiable desire for attention and recognition. Your task is to create a function that generates a 9-letter username that describes this type of person. You have an array of words that are commonly used to describe those who are attention-seeking and always want to be in the spotlight:
$words = array("egocentric", "narcissist", "showboater", "attention", "flamboyant", "exhibition", "self-lover", "grandiose", "cocky");
Your function should randomly select a word from this array and return it as the username. Can you create the code for this function? Remember, the username must be exactly 9 letters long. Good luck!

output:
Sure, here's the code for the function:
```
function generateUsername() {
  $words = array("egocentric", "narcissist", "showboater", "attention", "flamboyant", "exhibition", "self-lover", "grandiose", "cocky");
  $username = "";
  while(strlen($username) != 9) {
    $randomIndex = array_rand($words);
    $randomWord = $words[$randomIndex];
    if(strlen($randomWord) <= 9 - strlen($username)) {
      $username .= $randomWord;
    }
  }
  return $username;
}
```
This function uses a while loop to keep adding words to the username until it reaches exactly 9 characters. It randomly selects a word from the array using `array_rand()` and checks if it can fit in the remaining space in the username. If it can, it adds the word to the username. If not, it selects another word until it finds one that fits. Finally, it returns the generated username.

