const sum = uniqueArr.reduce((acc, curr) => acc + curr, 0);
const meanValue = sum / uniqueArr.length;
console.log("Processed array:", uniqueArr);
console.log("Highest value:", highestValue);
console.log("Lowest value:", lowestValue);
console.log("Mean value:", meanValue);
```
This code uses the spread operator and the Set object to eliminate repetitive elements, the sort() method to arrange the array in descending order, and simple arithmetic operations to compute the highest and lowest values and the mean value of the non-repeated elements. The code is efficient and can handle large arrays.

